MASTER AESTHETIC & SYSTEM RULES FOR TUI_OS (VAULT WORLDWIDE):
This is one continuous personal OS field — not a dashboard, not stacked sections.
No cards, rounded corners, soft shadows, section billboards, DateBlocks, or teal watermarks.

PALETTE: Canvas #F4F4F0 · Ink #111 · Cobalt #0000FF · Urgent #FF2B2B.
Cobalt = chrome. Red = strikes + URGENT + [X] only.

TYPE: JetBrains Mono everywhere except calendar numerals (Space Grotesk, light).

COMPOSITION (mobile-first):
1. Centered VAULT WORLDWIDE 90s-sleaze micrographic (scanline globe + orbital seal). No boxes around it.
2. Calendar block — Day 1 top-left continuous wrap, half-scale numerals, tight ungridded pack.
   Day labels = cobalt on white. Logged = red mid-strike over label. Selected logs = parasite chips.
   TUI toggle MONTH ↔ YEAR. Month view has ◀ ▶ nav. Year view = 12 mini months, same language.
3. Unix file-tree nest from hell — dense ASCII connectors (│ ├── └──). Click = nest context.
4. Scratch dump — cobalt date anchors, hairline rules. Click = dump context.
5. ONE fixed bottom Prompt Dock — always locked to viewport bottom. Context comes from what you click
   (day / nest node / dump). No mode chips or CTX boxes in the header. Never three forms.

HARD VETO: DateBlocks, jagged day cards, SaaS stacks, acid watermarks, giant boxed logos, demo fluff.
